cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below."
title: "nano-agent: A Tiny Model Beats Its Teacher — Verified-Loop Repair with a Sub-1B Language Model"
authors:
  - family-names: Ahmed
    given-names: Tanvir
repository-code: "https://github.com/mailtotanvir/nano-agent"
license: Apache-2.0
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-09-04"
keywords:
  - small language models
  - code repair
  - verified loop
  - knowledge distillation
  - Rust
  - curriculum learning
abstract: >
  A 0.5B-parameter code model placed inside a deterministic
  verify-propose-apply-reverify loop, with the Rust compiler as the oracle,
  repairs compiler errors at rates that exceed the mid-tier model used to
  generate its training data. An untrained model in the loop scores 0%; one SFT
  pass reaches 86.7% in-distribution. A failure-driven curriculum lifts frozen
  out-of-distribution accuracy from 44% to 60% (past the 56% teacher bar), and a
  stronger-teacher ablation raises it to 72%, bounded by a structural-insertion
  capacity limit. The model is one component; the verified recipe is the product.
